{
  "configuration_id": "config_012",
  "reason": "Evidence: Only one experiment is complete (config_001: rna_only, singleprofile, scgpt → acc 0.41, F1 0.38), giving a weak baseline with no information about whether the image modality carries any predictive signal. Question: Does image-only representation (resnet50, singleprofile, no aggregation/fusion) provide meaningful classification signal comparable to or complementary with RNA? Why this is the best next experiment: config_012 mirrors the structural simplicity of config_001 (singleprofile, no aggregation, no fusion) while swapping only the modality from RNA to image. This isolates the effect of modality as the single variable. Answering whether image alone has signal is the most fundamental uncertainty in a multimodal study: if image is weak, the search should focus on RNA encoder/aggregation improvements; if image is strong, multimodal fusion becomes a high-priority direction. This single experiment reduces the largest source of uncertainty in the design space before committing budget to more complex multimodal or multiprofile configurations."
}

